  "decisions": {
    "gripper": "Retain the stock AgileX assembly from yor-full-agx.mjcf. Its link7-to-palm and grasp transforms are preserved in Sophia. make_agx_variant.py explicitly labels the installed adapter offset as an estimate; source inheritance does not make it a hardware measurement.",
    "legacy_camera": "Do not transplant the Piper/iPhone camera transform. It is attached to a different 37342-triangle gripper_body mesh on a six-joint arm. The shared 12988-triangle stock housing is declared but unused in that camera assembly, so its matching filename is not a frame bridge.",
    "custom_camera_mounts": "L/R_Camera_Mount meshes belong to the custom articulated gripper assembly in yor-full.mjcf; that model defines no wrist optical camera. Retain these as alternative-assembly evidence.",
    "wrist": "Retain the existing palm-relative [42, 0, 52] mm and 10 degree toe-in as the accepted photo estimate. Existing robot photos and dataset support a board camera looking toward the task, but do not uniquely establish metric optical extrinsics. Supplied per-camera intrinsics remain applied.",
    "completion": "Frame/source reconciliation is complete. No supported numeric mounting correction was found; remaining uncertainty is an accepted simulation assumption, not a request for further measurements."
  },
